 "extract": "The Spanish sparrow or willow sparrow (Passer hispaniolensis) is a passerine bird of the sparrow family Passeridae. It is found in the Mediterranean region and south-west and central Asia. It is very similar to the closely related house sparrow, and the two species show their close relation in a \"biological mix-up\" of hybridisation in the Mediterranean region, which complicates the taxonomy of this species.",
